Keyless for Debian/Ubuntu
===============================

Install
-------

  sudo apt install ./keyless_<version>_amd64.deb

The package installs:

  /usr/bin/keyless                  CLI and UI launcher
  /opt/keyless/                     self-contained Python runtime
  /usr/share/applications/keyless.desktop
  /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/99-keyless-uinput.rules
  /usr/lib/systemd/user/keyless.service (optional, not enabled)

First run
---------

Open "Keyless" from the application menu. Setup:

  1. Permissions: camera, microphone, /dev/uinput, input devices, screen capture.
  2. Cameras: choose two stable /dev/v4l/by-id devices.
  3. Calibration: the full-screen target window.
  4. Speech: download the pinned Parakeet model (about 630 MB) or keep Whisper.
  5. Optional AI provider: OpenAI-compatible, Ollama, or an installed ACP agent.
  6. Practice: one contained click, then Start listening.

The /dev/uinput udev rule uses TAG+="uaccess", so the active desktop session gets
write access without a re-login.  If the rule is ignored, log out and back in.

Privacy
-------

Camera, speech, and history stay on this device.  A remote AI provider is optional
and is never selected automatically.  Screenshots are only sent to a remote gaze
VLM after the explicit "Allow screenshots to leave this device" consent.

Autostart (optional)
--------------------

  systemctl --user enable --now keyless.service

Uninstall
---------

  sudo apt remove keyless
  rm -rf ~/.local/share/keyless   # models, history (optional)
  rm -rf ~/.config/keyless        # settings, calibration (optional)
